01:09:08,571 --> 01:09:14,571
Challengers is a 2024 American romantic sports film directed by
Luca Guadagnino and written by Justin Kuritzkes.

12
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
It follows the love triangle among an injured tennis star-turned-coach (Zendaya), her low-circuit tennis player ex-boyfriend (Josh O'Connor), and her tennis
champion husband (Mike Faist) across 13 years of their relationship, culminating in the match between the two men on the ATP Challenger Tour.

13
01:21:42,857 --> 01:21:48,857
Kuritzkes' screenplay was acquired by MGM in February 2022, with the main cast and Guadagnino being hired shortly after; Zendaya,
O'Connor, and Faist trained for months with former tennis player and coach Brad Gilbert to prepare for their roles.

14
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
Principal photography ran from May to June 2022, primarily in Boston.

15
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
Sayombhu Mukdeeprom, who previously worked with Guadagnino on Call Me by Your
Name (2017) and Suspiria (2018), served as cinematographer.

16
01:40:34,285 --> 01:40:40,285
Delayed from an initial September 2023 release in response to the 2023 SAG-AFTRA strike, Challengers premiered in Sydney on
March 26, 2024, and was theatrically released in the United States by Amazon MGM Studios one month later.

17
01:46:51,428 --> 01:46:57,428
It grossed $96 million worldwide and received critical acclaim.

18
01:53:08,571 --> 01:53:14,571
Among the film's accolades were four nominations at the 82nd Golden Globe Awards (including
Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy), where it won Best Original Score.

19
01:59:25,714 --> 01:59:31,714
The film explores themes of infidelity, husband wife
relationship, love triangle, sports, tennis.

20
02:05:42,857 --> 02:05:48,857
The tone is emotional.
